Notice.Description:
Ofgem is seeking a consultancy or consortium to act as a strategic analytical partner to provide specialist economic, econometric and cost modelling advice to support the development and delivery of the ED3 electricity distribution price control, with additional call-off support for RIIO3 and preparatory work for the future RIIO4 framework where required.
    Under this contract, the supplier will provide specialist economic and econometric support to enable the development and delivery of ED3. This includes advising on the framework, reviewing methodological choices, and supporting Ofgem's cost assessment and detailed scrutiny of network company business plans. The supplier will evaluate the efficiency and justification of proposed expenditure and outputs, assess how companies address uncertainty and scenario driven cost variations, and test the coherence and deliverability of business plans. They may also support the design and calibration of outputs, incentives and uncertainty mechanisms, as well as provide analytical or advisory input in the event of any appeals following Final Determinations.
    In addition to ED3, the supplier may be commissioned to provide wider economic advice across RIIO 3 and preparatory work for RIIO 4. This may include:
    * support with RIIO 3 outputs, incentives and re-openers
    * analytical work underpinning the transition to more digital, structured and AI enabled approaches to cost assessment and price control design; and
    * strategic adv...nal or ad hoc RIIO/ED3 related work will be commissioned under the contract rate card.
    * Meetings, Clarifications and Publication Requirements
    The supplier will be required to:
    * maintain a clear, detailed and transparent audit trail for all analysis, raw data, assumptions and models;
    * provide all models and analytical outputs to Ofgem at relevant milestones;
    * where required, attend meetings with Ofgem teams, the Ofgem Board (GEMA) and, network companies;
    * Attend stakeholder working groups, create and present materials; and
    * provide advice and explanation of recommendations, and support Ofgem throughout internal challenge processes.
    All outputs produced under this contract - including models, reports, advice and other materials should be suitable for external use and publication, including on the Ofgem website and within documents used in any Competition Markets Authority (CMA) appeal, judicial review or other challenge. Unless made clear by Ofgem as part of the associated work order.
    * Support During Appeals or Challenges
    In the event of any appeal following ED3 Final Determinations, the supplier may be required to:
    * assist Ofgem in reviewing and responding to appellant arguments;
    * replicate or stress test modelling submitted by network companies;
    * prepare technical evidence for Ofgem's legal teams and Counsel;
    * contribute to analytical content required for the CMA process;
    * be a part of the appeal hearing to defend relevant technical work.

Further competition using Government Commercial Agency (GCA), Management Consultancy Four Framework (MCF4) (RM6309) Lot 4: Finance.

          Background
          As with many other sectors, the Business Retail Market is constituted such that Retailers can choose to 'pre-pay' or 'post-pay' Wholesalers for services. Whenever post-pay is used, there is the risk that a Retailer may default on payment for services they have already received from the Wholesaler. To mitigate the potential impact of this risk, a set of Credit and Collateral Arrangements (CCAs) were developed prior to market opening and are set out within the market codes which help govern and underpin the Business Retail Market.

          We are currently reviewing these CCA arrangements with a view to understanding if and where they are delivering for customers and the market, and if, and how recommendations for amendment or change may be warranted. We published in May 2026 a CCA Consultation which set out our initial proposals for change, including an accompanying supporting quantitative spreadsheet. We now wish to move to Stage 2 which is to develop and publish a Decision document on our proposed changes.

          Scope
          Ofwat is seeking external advice for stage 2 of its work on the review of the CCA review.

          The successful bidder will provide specialist regulatory and policy advice to assist Ofwat in developing final policy positions and preparing final decision materials following completion of the consultation process. Expert advice will include analysis of consultation responses; identification of key themes and evidence; assessment and evaluation of policy options; use, development and quality assurance of quantitative modelling spreadsheet(s); and help in drafting final decision papers and supporting materials.

          Ofwat will retain responsibility for reaching conclusions on consultation submissions and policy choices as set out in final decision documents and materials.

          The successful bidder will advise Ofwat by:
          •	providing independent expert advice and challenge on emerging policy positions;
          •	assisting with the development and refinement of policy options;
          •	assist in developing and quality assuring and challenging quantitative modelling spreadsheet(s);
          •	assessing implementation considerations, risks and unintended consequences associated with potential changes;
          •	expert advice on the development of decision-making materials for internal governance;
          •	drafting and reviewing final decision papers and supporting documents;
          •	providing quality assurance of written outputs; and
          •	attending project meetings and workshops as required.

          The project has commenced and advice is needed from September 2026 until the end of February 2027.

The key dates for this RFI are as follows:

